{"slug":"greg-stanton","qid":"Q5606289","name":"Greg Stanton","desc":"American lawyer and politician (born 1970)","article":"Greg Stanton","born":"1970-03-08","died":null,"birthplace":"Long Island","parties":["Democratic Party"],"offices":[{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"AZ-04","f":2023,"u":null},{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"AZ-09","f":2019,"u":2023},{"t":"Mayor of Phoenix","w":"","f":2012,"u":2018}],"summary":"Gregory John Stanton (born March 8, 1970) is an American lawyer and politician who is the U.S. representative from Arizona's 4th congressional district, serving since 2019. A Democrat, he was previously mayor of Phoenix from 2012 to 2018, and was on the Phoenix City Council from 2000 until 2009.\nStanton was elected mayor in 2011 and reelected in 2015.","photo":{"f":"greg-stanton.jpg","by":"House Creative Services","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":null,"page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Greg_Stanton_119th_Congress.jpg"},"history":[{"y":2026,"o":"H","k":"AZ-04","p":"D","n":"Greg Stanton","race":"AZ-04"},{"y":2024,"o":"H","k":"AZ-04","p":"D","v":176428,"s":52.74,"w":true,"n":"Greg Stanton"},{"y":2022,"o":"H","k":"AZ-04","p":"D","v":148941,"s":56.1,"w":true,"n":"Greg Stanton"},{"y":2020,"o":"H","k":"AZ-09","p":"D","v":217094,"s":61.63,"w":true,"n":"Greg Stanton"},{"y":2018,"o":"H","k":"AZ-09","p":"D","v":159583,"s":61.09,"w":true,"n":"Greg Stanton"}]}